      "worked_solution": "We want to express the area $\\mathcal{A}$ between the function $f(x) = -2x^3+2$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=0$ and $x=1.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x) = -2x^3+2$ between the lower limit $x=0$ and the upper limit $x=1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\mathcal{A} = \\int_0^1 (-2x^3+2)\\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$",
